WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.280
A hunter shoots one of a pair of cranes.

2
00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.220
A sage watches its mate cry out.

3
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.820
His grief pours out as
a verse: by tradition,

4
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.350
the first verse of the Ramayana.

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.520
The Bhagavad Gita says
the wise see a priest,

6
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.430
a cow, an elephant and a dog as all one.

7
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.030
If every living being has a soul,
how do Hindus decide about abortion,

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.740
meat, gene editing and marriage?

9
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.800
In this mission, you'll look at Hindu
teaching on the start and end of life,

10
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.470
and on animals.

11
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.610
Then you'll explore marriage
and gender in Hindu texts,

12
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.570
and in Indian law.

13
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.680
Your mission: find out how Hindus apply
their principles to these modern issues.
